{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af163d2","nodeId":"yGRQcx64S-yBGEoOeMc55","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# Dockerfile\n\nA Dockerfile is a text document that contains a list of instructions used by the Docker engine to build an image. Each instruction in the Dockerfile adds a new layer to the image. Docker will build the image based on these instructions, and then you can run containers from the image.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Dockerfile Reference","url":"https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba75"},{"type":"official","title":"Dockerfile Best Practices","url":"https://docs.docker.com/develop/develop-images/dockerfile_best-practices/","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba76"},{"type":"opensource","title":"Dockerfile Examples","url":"https://github.com/dockersamples","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba77"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/yGRQcx64S-yBGEoOeMc55.md"}